both have same content , that  is known as Interning . str and grt
have same address.

why ? we have to save space

String x = new String("Hello");
To avoid interning we using new keyword in java

String s = "Hello";
String x = "Hello";
 x = "cello";
Initially there are pointing to same address but when we write the
x = "cello" then are pointing to different address because string
are immutable.




